PARITY — the native surface reproduces the web SwipeRow data, composition, states & i18n:
[x] Swipe-to-action row wrapper (web `children` → generic `Content`): a ZStack lays the left/right edge
    action panels behind the foreground row and translates it by the live drag offset, reproducing the
    iOS Mail / Notes interaction.
[x] Drag math is the pure web logic in `SwipeRowGeometry`: 8px horizontal axis-lock, vertical-drift
    cancel so the parent list keeps scrolling, wired-side + ±width overshoot clamp, the
    reveal-threshold (64px) crossing, and the release ladder — auto-fire past half width / peek past
    threshold (rest at ±ACTION_WIDTH 96px) / snap closed. All asserted by unit tests.
[x] One-shot haptic the first time the reveal threshold is crossed (web `navigator.vibrate(10)`) via
    `.sensoryFeedback(.impact, trigger:)`.
[x] Touch-only by default (web `enabled ?? useIsCoarsePointer()`): on a fine pointer (macOS default,
    or host `enabled:false`) the row is a straight pass-through with NO gesture — the web `!active`
    branch. The coarse-pointer capability binds through the P1/S8 state-holder.
[x] Reduce Motion collapses the snap-back animation to an instant transition (web
    `prefers-reduced-motion`) via `@Environment(\.accessibilityReduceMotion)` — the `useMotionPreference`
    binding at the view boundary.
[x] Action tone → token + default SF Symbol parity (web `defaultIcon` / `actionPanelClasses`):
    danger → statusDanger + `trash` (web Trash2/rose); default → accent + `archivebox` (web Archive/cyan).
[x] P4 leaf states the web pure render lacks (treated like the sibling wrapper surface
    SectionErrorBoundary 0138): loading (skeleton row), empty (no row → friendly card, never blank),
    error (QueryError + Retry), plus the orthogonal freshness axis — stale/offline chip + banner with a
    one-shot stale auto-refresh. The wrapped row is the `content` phase.
[x] Hooks bind via the shared P1/S8 state-holder seam (SwipeRowSource + SwipeRowModel); NO direct HTTP
    in the view (the web source has none — it owns no data).
[x] i18n: the web source resolves ZERO `t()` keys (anonymous surface; action labels arrive
    host-localized via `SwipeAction.label`, exactly like the native `SwipeAction.label`). The 13 keys
    in SwipeRow.strings (table "SwipeRow") are native chrome (a11y + leaf states + freshness). No
    English string literals in native code — all via the P1/S10 facade.
[x] Accessibility: the swipe row is one VoiceOver element exposing each wired action as a custom action
    (`.accessibilityActions`) + an "Actions available" hint, so the hidden gesture is fully operable
    without a swipe; the edge buttons carry resolved labels (web `ariaLabel ?? label`).
[x] Telemetry: `view.opened` emitted once with surface slug "SwipeRow" (P1/S11 seam; asserted by
    testStartEmitsViewOpenedOnceEvenAcrossRestart).
[x] No TODO/stub/mock/placeholder/Lorem in shipped code.

